# Wave I.1 — Owner-settings panel lazy loader

## Problem

Wave H moved the Urban owner settings **panel SoT** into `@app-tour/workspace-urban` and neutralized the route (`/settings/workspace-owner`). The shell page still had a **static** product import:

```ts
import { WorkspaceOwnerSettingsPanel } from "@app-tour/workspace-urban/host/settings/owner-panel";
```

That keeps Urban in the admin compile graph even when the tenant is not Urban — the first thin-shell debt for this surface.

## Decision

1. Declare the panel module on the Urban manifest under `operatorShell.ownerSettingsPanel`:

```json
"ownerSettingsPanel": {
  "module": "@app-tour/workspace-urban/host/settings/owner-panel",
  "exportName": "WorkspaceOwnerSettingsPanel"
}
```

2. Codegen [`apps/web/src/bootstrap/workspace-owner-settings-panel-loaders.generated.ts`](../../apps/web/src/bootstrap/workspace-owner-settings-panel-loaders.generated.ts) from manifests (same switch/`import()` pattern as plugin loaders).

3. [`apps/web/app/(app)/settings/workspace-owner/page.tsx`](../../apps/web/app/(app)/settings/workspace-owner/page.tsx) loads the panel via `loadWorkspaceOwnerSettingsPanel(pluginId)` — **no** static `@app-tour/workspace-urban` import.

4. Host injection (`apiBaseUrl`, auth headers, i18n labels) and Phase 8 canLoad stay unchanged.

## Out of scope

- Removing `@app-tour/workspace-urban` from `apps/web/package.json` (install isolation — later Wave)
- Static `@app-tour/workspace-starter` shell imports → [`wave-i-2-sdk-starter-shell.mdoc`](./wave-i-2-sdk-starter-shell.mdoc) (Wave I.2)
- Deleting `wizard/denali/*` firewall
- Renaming Urban canLoad policy ids

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm run guard:workspace-registry-fresh
pnpm run wave-i0:guard
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-i-1-owner-settings-lazy-loader.spec.ts \
  test/wave-h-urban-owner-panel-package.spec.ts \
  test/wave-h-workspace-owner-shell-typing.spec.ts
```
